  -> THE MLM CONSTRUCTION HAS NO SINGLE-TOKEN ATTRACTOR (2 models, top-1 9.9-11.3%), against the AR rule's 74.4% on the same threshold. The degeneracy belongs to the AR two-token rule, not to iterated resampling on token lattices. Phase 3's MLM results used this construction and are not undermined by F65; a second paper should be built on the MLM path rather than the AR universality programme. ar-bos vs ar-none: 24.1% vs 74.4% (-50.3 points). A single BOS token materially changes it, which implicates the prompt being out of distribution.

